<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37710" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-lūceo</span></b> , xi, 2, v.
			n.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To shine</i> or <i>give light before;
				to hold</i> or <i>carry a light before</i>, <i>to light.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Of those who carry a
			light: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servus praelucens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 1, 2, 89</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Of
			the light itself: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeluxere faces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 42, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne ignis noster praeluceat facinori,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 4, 11, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> In gen., <i>to shine forth</i>, <i>be bright</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amicitia bonā spe praelucet in
					posterum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Lael. 7, 23</span></i>
			.—With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lumenque tuae praeluceo vitae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 4, 95</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> In
			partic., <i>to shine brighter</i>, <i>to
				outshine</i>, <i>surpass</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nullus sinus Baiis praelucet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 1, 83</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To shine very much</i>, <i>shine
				brightly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">baculum praelucet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					32, 10, 52, § 141</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
